      "kind": "modify",
      "field": "remaining_path",
      "edits": [
        {
          "modify_from": "First identify the starting target and the chronological sequence of arrivals at adjacent target sites through the final demonstration arrival.",
          "modify_to": "First construct a temporary traversal ledger from the demonstration alone, excluding the reset to the execution starting scene. Identify the starting target and every chronological arrival through the final demonstration arrival, identifying sites by stable horizontal order rather than exact fluctuating coordinates. Each consecutive pair of distinct adjacent sites creates one ledger row, even if that pair or destination has appeared before. Complete this arrival ledger before classifying any traversal; never compress its repeated rows. The ledger is temporary reasoning at this decision, not an additional memory field."
        },
        {
          "modify_from": "Second classify each traversal independently. Compute destination target x minus departure target x, and judge the intermediate wrist trajectory relative to the line joining the wrist resting positions at those two sites. Upper means smaller image y than that baseline at the corresponding x; lower means larger image y.",
          "modify_to": "Second classify each ledger row independently. For that crossing, identify its departure and destination target sites, representative resting wrist positions at those endpoints, and intermediate wrist samples belonging to that crossing. Write any positions as [y, x]. Compute destination target x minus departure target x to determine horizontal direction; do not use a local reversal in wrist x. Judge the arc using the substantial interior wrist excursion relative to the line joining that row's endpoint wrist positions, not a near-arrival sample that may belong to the next crossing. For endpoint wrist positions [y0, x0] and [y1, x1] and an interior wrist sample [ys, xs], when x1 differs from x0, baseline_y = y0 + (y1 - y0) * (xs - x0) / (x1 - x0). Negative ys minus baseline_y indicates upper; positive indicates lower. Use wrist coordinates throughout this baseline calculation. Reversing horizontal direction does not by itself change the side of the baseline occupied by the arc."
        },
        {
          "modify_from": "Write one letter per adjacent-site traversal in chronological order, and verify that the number of letters equals the number of traversals identified in the first stage, including the traversal ending at the final arrival.",
          "modify_to": "Write exactly one letter per ledger row in chronological order. Verify a one-to-one correspondence between rows and letters, retaining every repeated crossing and the row ending at the final demonstration arrival."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "subgoal_execution_plan": [],
